WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:02.469
- [Narrator] There's no Chinese alphabet.

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:07.258
Instead, each word is represented
by a symbol or character.

00:00:07.258 --> 00:00:09.412
(air whooshing)

00:00:09.412 --> 00:00:14.412
- How on Earth did a language
with tens of thousands

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:17.293
of characters fit onto this keyboard?

00:00:17.293 --> 00:00:20.180
- [Narrator] Here is a
world of communication,

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.298
tailored for your needs
of today and tomorrow.

00:00:23.298 --> 00:00:26.570
- [Narrator] What really accounts
for China's meteoric rise

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:28.540
as a major global power?

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.300
- This is Shenzhen.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.230
It's a city in the south of China.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:33.480
I've actually been there.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:35.820
But back in the 1980s,

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.240
this was just a sleepy fishing village

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.620
with less than, like 100,000 people.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.240
Today, it is home to 12.5 million people,

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.250
a giant metropolis with huge buildings

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:50.720
and home to some of the
largest tech companies

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:52.370
on the planet.

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:56.180
This city is emblematic of
China's technological rise

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:57.540
over the last 40 years.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:59.890
It's an explosion in
technology and development

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:03.150
that has really never happened
before in human history.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:06.292
From an agrarian society to
a technological powerhouse

00:01:06.292 --> 00:01:08.248
in just a couple of decades.

00:01:08.248 --> 00:01:09.210
- That's fast.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.510
- This almost didn't happen.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:15.350
China almost didn't become
the technological powerhouse.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:17.340
And what held them back is something

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:18.720
I have thought about a lot,

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:21.170
which is this keyboard.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:24.050
This keyboard has like, 80 or so keys,

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.040
and the Chinese language has like

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.640
tens of thousands of characters.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.280
So how did they fit their
language onto this keyboard?

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:32.300
To answer that question,

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:35.170
you have to dive deep into modern China,

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:37.390
into Chairman Mao,

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:40.650
into the divide between
Taiwan and mainland China,

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:43.010
who despite speaking the same language

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:45.230
use very different typing methods,

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:47.460
all because of geopolitics.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.870
It's a story of how China took a keyboard

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:53.000
that was developed for a vastly
different language system

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.770
and mastered it, mastered it better

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:56.690
than we did here in the West.

00:01:56.690 --> 00:01:59.030
It's a fascinating story
of culture and history

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.905
and technology, and I
want to share it with you.

00:02:01.905 --> 00:02:03.091
- [Narrator] Here is China.

00:02:03.091 --> 00:02:04.080
- [Narrator] It's become a keystone

