00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:41.410
- So basically growing up
as a Chinese or Taiwanese,

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:45.640
you have to learn how to
write those characters.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.920
That's kind of the first thing first.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:51.790
And then you learn the, like
the pronunciation system

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:54.050
behind all the characters.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:57.860
And in China, that's pinyin,
and in Taiwan, that's zhuyin.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:59.535
- So let's break this down.

00:02:59.535 --> 00:03:03.410
Most languages are
written with an alphabet.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:06.280
Each letter in that
alphabet represents a sound.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:10.240
And when you string those sounds
together, you make a word.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.600
It seems so intuitive as if like

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.000
this is the only way to do it.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.370
But in Chinese,

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:16.580
- There's another way.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:20.070
- Chinese uses complex
characters for each word,

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.470
so every word is a character.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:25.490
Each one of these characters
represents a different thing,

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:28.750
an object, the feeling, a concept, a verb.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.216
All in all, there're
upwards of 70 or 80 thousand

00:03:31.216 --> 00:03:33.500
of these characters.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.350
This system was just fine.

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:37.500
It worked in China for a really long time

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:41.440
because you can use a brush
or a pen to write stuff out.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:44.612
- I like that. It's like if
it ain't broke, don't fix it.

00:03:44.612 --> 00:03:47.300
- This is the qwerty keyboard.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.880
It's called the qwerty keyboard

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:51.453
because I mean, just look at it.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:57.030
This is the mechanism to which
people not just communicate

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:59.410
with each other, but code the world,

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:02.750
the software and programs
that we all use all the time.

